#!/usr/bin/env dyalogscript
⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
⍝ resolver.apls
⍝ A mini nslookup written in pure APL: prints every IPv4 and IPv6 address of a host name.
⍝ It resolves names on its own with this steps:
⍝   1. it looks for the name in /etc/hosts
⍝   2. if it is not there, it asks the DNS servers listed in /etc/resolv.conf inorder
⍝ There is no getaddrinfo here :( you need ot build the DNS query bytes handmade
⍝ send them over TCP to port 53 of the DNS server and decode the reply bytes
⍝ Usage: dyalogscript resolver.apls google.com
⍝ Compare with: dig www.usb.ve   and   dig AAAA www.usb.ve
⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

                          ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
'Conga' ⎕CY 'conga'       ⍝ copy the networking library conga
DRC←Conga.Init ''         ⍝ start conga. Vamo' negro pa la conga
⎕IO←0                     ⍝ index origin 0 like in C
