⍝ ---------- argv processing ----------
⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

                                     ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
∇ r←Args;all;m                       ⍝ arguments that come after the script name
 all←2 ⎕NQ '.' 'GetCommandLineArgs'  ⍝ the whole command line, as a list of strings
 m←{'.apls'≡¯5↑⍵}¨all                ⍝ 1 where the element is the path of the script
 :If ~∨/m                            ⍝ the script path was not found
     r←⍬                             ⍝ an empty list: no arguments
 :Else                               ⍝ the script path was found
     r←(1+⊃⍸m)↓all                   ⍝ everything after the script path
 :EndIf                              ⍝ close of the if
∇
                                     ⍝ DONT COMMENT UP (it crashes for the close of the func)
                                     ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
⍝ ---------- step 1: /etc/hosts ----------
⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

                                        ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
∇ found←HostsFile name;lines;line;w;ip  ⍝ print the addresses of name listed in /etc/hosts
 found←0                                ⍝ 0 = not found yet
 :Trap 0                                ⍝ if the file cannot be read, just say "not found"
     lines←⊃⎕NGET '/etc/hosts' 1        ⍝ the file as a list of lines
 :Else                                  ⍝ reading failed
     :Return                            ⍝ leave with found = 0
 :EndTrap                               ⍝ close of the trap
 :For line :In lines                    ⍝ lines like "127.0.0.1 localhost localhost.localdomain"
     line←(∧\line≠'#')/line             ⍝ ignore everything after a '#' (comments)
     w←Words line                       ⍝ first word = IP, the rest = names
     :If (2≤≢w)∧(⊂⎕C name)∊⎕C 1↓w       ⍝ our name is one of the names (ignoring case)
         ip←⊃w                          ⍝ the IP of that line
         :If ':'∊ip                     ⍝ IPv6 addresses contain ':'
             ⎕←'IPv6 ',ip               ⍝ print it as IPv6
         :Else                          ⍝ otherwise it is IPv4
             ⎕←'IPv4 ',ip               ⍝ print it as IPv4
         :EndIf                         ⍝ close of the if
         found←1                        ⍝ we found at least one address
     :EndIf                             ⍝ close of the if
 :EndFor                                ⍝ close of the for
∇
                                        ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
⍝ ---------- step 2: /etc/resolv.conf ----------
⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

                                        ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
∇ list←NameServers;lines;line;w         ⍝ every "nameserver" line of /etc/resolv.conf, in order
 list←⍬                                 ⍝ start with an emtpy list
 :Trap 0                                ⍝ if the file cannot be read, keep theempty list
     lines←⊃⎕NGET '/etc/resolv.conf' 1  ⍝ the file as a list of lines
     :For line :In lines                ⍝ look at each line
         w←Words line                   ⍝ example "nameserver" "127.0.0.53"
         :If ('nameserver'≡⊃w)∧2≤≢w     ⍝ it is a nameserver line
             list,←⊂1⊃w                 ⍝ add the second word (the server's IP) to the list
         :EndIf                         ⍝ close of the if
     :EndFor                            ⍝ next line
 :EndTrap                               ⍝ close of the trap
 :If 0=≢list                            ⍝ no nameserver lines at all
     list←,⊂'127.0.0.1'                 ⍝ same default as the C library: this machine
 :EndIf                                 ⍝ close of the if
∇
                                        ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
⍝ ---------- step 3: DNS Query ---------
⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

                                         ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
∇ msg←name BuildQuery type;labels;qname  ⍝ query for name; type 1 = A (IPv4), 28 = AAAA (IPv6)
 labels←'.'(≠⊆⊢)name                     ⍝ split '.'
 qname←(∊{(≢⍵),⎕UCS ⍵}¨labels),0         ⍝ each label as length byte + its bytes, then a 0 byte
 msg←(U16 ?65536)                        ⍝ ID is a random 16-bit number
 msg,←1 0                                ⍝ flags
 msg,←0 1,0 0,0 0,0 0                    ⍝ 1 question, 0 answers, 0 authority, 0 additional
 msg,←qname,(U16 type),U16 1             ⍝ the question: name, type, class 1
∇
                                         ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
⍝ ------- step 4: Query over TCP ---------
⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

                                                        ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
∇ reply←server Query msg;r;rc;c;obj;evt;data;buf;tries  ⍝ reply bytes, or ⍬ if this server failed
 reply←⍬                                                ⍝ empty until we get an answer
 r←DRC.Clt '' server 53 'Raw'                           ⍝ connect to port 53 in Raw mode
 (rc c)←2↑r                                             ⍝ rc = 0 if OK; c = name of the con
 :If rc≠0                                               ⍝ could not connect to this server
     :Return                                            ⍝ leave with an empty reply: main tries
 :EndIf                                                 ⍝ the next server. Close of the if
 rc←⊃DRC.Send c ((U16≢msg),msg)                         ⍝ over TCP, DNS messages start with 2 bytes
 buf←⍬                                                  ⍝ here we collect the bytes that arrive
 tries←0                                                ⍝ how many 100 ms waits without data
 :While tries<50                                        ⍝ give up after about 5 seconds
     (rc obj evt data)←4↑DRC.Wait c 100                 ⍝ wait up to 100 ms for an event
     :If rc=0                                           ⍝ something happened
         :If (⊂evt)∊'Block' 'BlockLast'                 ⍝ data arrived
             buf,←256|data                              ⍝ append the bytes that arrived
         :EndIf                                         ⍝ close of the if
     :ElseIf rc=100                                     ⍝ 100 = timeout, nothing arrived yet
         tries+←1                                       ⍝ count one more wait
     :Else                                              ⍝ the connection was closed or failed
         :Leave                                         ⍝ stop waiting
     :EndIf                                             ⍝ close of the if
     :If (2≤≢buf)∧(≢buf)≥2+256⊥2↑buf                    ⍝ TCP is a byte stream: stop when
         :Leave                                         ⍝ we have the full reply
     :EndIf                                             ⍝ close of the if
 :EndWhile                                              ⍝ keep waiting
 {}DRC.Close c                                          ⍝ close the TCP connection (sent FIN)
 reply←2↓buf                                            ⍝ drop the 2-byte lenght
∇
                                                        ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
⍝ ------ step 5: format ans ----------
⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

                                            ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
∇ txt←IPv6 bytes;g;h;z;runs;best;n          ⍝ 16 bytes is an IPv6, longest run of zeros as "::"
 g←256⊥⍉8 2⍴bytes                           ⍝ 8 groups of 16 bits
 h←Hex¨g                                    ⍝ each group in hexdec
 z←0=g                                      ⍝ 1 where the group is zero
 runs←(⊂z){+/∧\⍵↓⍺}¨⍳8                      ⍝ zero groups in a row starting at each position
 best←⊃⍒runs                                ⍝ where the longest run starts
 n←runs[best]                               ⍝ how long it is
 :If n<2                                    ⍝ no run worth compressing
     txt←Join h                             ⍝ write all 8 groups
 :Else                                      ⍝ there is a run of 2 or more zero groups
     txt←(Join best↑h),'::',Join(best+n)↓h  ⍝ groups before "::" groups after
 :EndIf                                     ⍝ close of the if
∇
                                            ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

                                    ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
∇ Show reply;qd;an;p;i;t;len;rdata  ⍝ print the A and AAAA records of a reply
 qd←256⊥reply[4 5]                  ⍝ number of questions
 an←256⊥reply[6 7]                  ⍝ number of answers
 p←12                               ⍝ the header is 12 bytes long
 :For i :In ⍳qd                     ⍝ skip each question
     p←4+reply SkipName p           ⍝ name + type + class
 :EndFor                            ⍝ next question
 :For i :In ⍳an                     ⍝ walk each answer
     p←reply SkipName p             ⍝ the answers name
     t←256⊥reply[p+0 1]             ⍝ record type
     len←256⊥reply[p+8 9]           ⍝ data length (after type, class and TTL)
     rdata←reply[p+10+⍳len]         ⍝ the record data
     p←p+10+len                     ⍝ position of the next answer
     :If (t=1)∧len=4                ⍝ A record is an IPv4 address
         ⎕←'IPv4 ',IPv4 rdata       ⍝ binary to text
     :ElseIf (t=28)∧len=16          ⍝ AAAA record is an IPv6 address
         ⎕←'IPv6 ',IPv6 rdata       ⍝ binary to text
     :EndIf                         ⍝ other types (e.g. CNAME = 5) are skipped
 :EndFor                            ⍝ next answer
∇
                                    ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
⍝ ---------- main ----------
⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

                                                       ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
∇ Main;args;name;server;r4;r6;rcode                    ⍝ the program starts here
 args←Args                                             ⍝ the command line arguments
 :If 1≠≢args                                           ⍝ we need exactly one: the host name
     ⎕←'usage: dyalogscript resolver.apls <hostname>'  ⍝ explain how to use it
     ⎕OFF 1                                            ⍝ exit with error code 1
 :EndIf                                                ⍝ close of the if
 name←⊃args                                            ⍝ the name to resolve
 :If HostsFile name                                    ⍝ step 1 if found in /etc/hosts
     :Return                                           ⍝ done, just like getaddrinfo
 :EndIf                                                ⍝ close of the if
 r4←⍬                                                  ⍝ no reply yet
 :For server :In NameServers                           ⍝ step 2 try each DNS server in order
     r4←server Query name BuildQuery 1                 ⍝ steps 3-4 ask for IPv4 addresses
     :If 12≤≢r4                                        ⍝ this server answered
         :Leave                                        ⍝ keep using this server
     :EndIf                                            ⍝ close of the if
 :EndFor                                               ⍝ try the next server
 :If 12>≢r4                                            ⍝ no server answered
     ⎕←name,': no DNS server answered'                 ⍝ explain the error
     ⎕OFF 1                                            ⍝ exit with error code 1
 :EndIf                                                ⍝ close of the if
 rcode←16|r4[3]                                        ⍝ low 4 bits of byte 3 = response code
 :If rcode≠0                                           ⍝ the server reported an error
     ⎕←name,': ',RcodeText rcode                       ⍝ e.g. "name does not exist (NXDOMAIN)"
     ⎕OFF 1                                            ⍝ exit with error code 1
 :EndIf                                                ⍝ close of the if
 r6←server Query name BuildQuery 28                    ⍝ same server, now ask for IPv6 addresses
 Show r4                                               ⍝ step 5: print the IPv4 addresses
 :If 12≤≢r6                                            ⍝ the IPv6 query got a reply
     Show r6                                           ⍝ print the IPv6 addresses
 :EndIf                                                ⍝ close of the if
∇
                                                       ⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

Main
⎕OFF
